## implementation summary
- scripts/r169_report_v5.py: GATE_MAX_PROVIDER_ERROR_SHARE=0.10, GATE_REQUIRE_FULL_COVERAGE=True;
  agreement() reports records/split_cases/missing_cases/duplicate_records/provider_error_share;
  gate() adds checks coverage==100% and provider_error_share<=0.10 plus data_sufficient; valid=false on breach.
- PREREGISTRATION.md §3.1 (pre-registered BEFORE freeze): full per-run coverage + <=10% provider errors;
  breach => 'inconclusive — insufficient data' regardless of agreement; no in-place completion of a broken run.
- synthetic deterministic test runs (monkeypatched tmp dirs, no network, no repo pollution):
  full-coverage run with 5 provider errors (4.2%) => data_sufficient=true, valid=true;
  run missing 18 records => data_sufficient=false, valid=false;
  run with 20 provider errors (16.9%) => data_sufficient=false, valid=false.
